SUMMARY:Chester County Horse-Shoe and More Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this point to point hike in rural Chester County Pennsylvania\
 , featuring some prominent trails including the Horse-Shoe Trail\, as well
  as other connections!\nI have planned this one specifically because it is
  a Sunday that hunting isn't permitted in some of the preserves along the 
 way\, and because most of the route is pleasant but within safety zones.\n
 After meeting at Bryn Coed\, we will shuttle with as few vehicles as possi
 ble to our start point\, at Highland Farm Park.\nWe'll start by walking so
 me of the trails to the north\, through fields and a wood line\, out into 
 a development.\nWe'll cut through the development and then out to the Pick
 ering Creek Trail.\nWe'll take the Station Blvd Trail north to the Eagle F
 arms Trail east\, then turn onto the pleasant Chester Springs Road.\nThe l
 ightly trafficked road will lead us to the Horse-Shoe Trail where we last 
 left off on it.\nWe'll follow Horse-Shoe Trail east for a bit\, and then t
 urn off at Bodine Road.\nWe'll follow a short road bit to the Hickory Trai
 l which takes us north more.\nFrom the Elbow Road\, we'll reach the Binky 
 Lee Preserve and pass through fields and woods. We'll exit the north side 
 from that\, and then follow some more back roads for a bit.\nLightly used 
 Kimberton Road and Flint Road will take us to Bryn Coed Preserve for the l
 ast leg of the hike.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 8374\nDistance wil
 l be about 15 miles.
