SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261128T073021Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270101T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270101T180000
SUMMARY:First Day Phillipsburg Easton Hike!
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this big loop hike featuring Easton and Phillipsburg!\nIt has 
 become a tradition doing this area as part of the New Year\, starting it o
 ff right with walking!\nThis year\, we'll do trails and historic sites all
  around both Easton and Phillipsburg\, and we'll start in Easton at the Gi
 ant Supermarket just off of Sullivan Trail.\nWe'll walk some back streets 
 for a bit tracing the historic route of the area trolley. This will lead u
 s into Gollub Park where we will visit the former site of the Paxinosa Inn
 \, and then make our way down along the trolley bed as it weaves around pa
 st St Anthony's Nose\, then return to the streets.\nWe'll pass through the
  college campus and down the giant steps that have been repaired recently\
 , then head across the Rt 22 bridge to Phillipsburg.\nWe'll follow Warren 
 Highlands Trail route and possibly just take in South Main Street past the
  historic railroad features. If your friends at any of these locations are
  around\, we'll be sure to stop in!\nWe continue from here across the blac
 k bridge and over to the former Morris Canal basin and Mt Parnassus. Depen
 ding on time\, we may go up the mountain for the view.\nWe'll make our way
  along the former Morris Canal back toward Union Square where we will cros
 s the Northampton Street Free Bridge into Easton.\nNext\, we follow greenw
 ays west into town\, mostly rail beds\, then north on the Easton and North
 ern line. We'll turn off and get on more of the Two Rivers Trailways to ge
 t back to Giant.\nTotal distance should be 15 miles.\nIf needed\, contact 
 me at 908 343 8374
